' Built-in `collections` package implementation (plan-01-functions.md §6.4).
' These generic functions are injected when a project imports `collections`.
' A user call `collections::sort(x)` is rewritten to `__collections_sort(x)`
' during monomorphization, so each is instantiated like any generic function.
'
' The native list/map members (`get`, `set`, `append`, `transform`, ...) moved
' out of the bare global namespace into `collections::` (plan-01-functions.md §5),
' so this implementation imports the package and qualifies those calls. `len(...)`
' stays a global builtin. The internal `__collections_slice` helper is a plain
' top-level function and is called unqualified.
IMPORT collections

' Stable bottom-up merge sort — O(n log n). Equal elements keep their original
' order (a right-run element is taken only when strictly less than the left-run
' element), matching the previous insertion sort's stability and ascending order.
'@@MFB_BODY:sort@@

' --- internal helpers ---------------------------------------------------------

' bug-306 S4: this body is DEAD -- `slice` is natively lowered as a bulk range copy,
' and the native path is what clamps `start` into [0, len] and `stop` into
' [start, len]. This source does not clamp, so it is not a usable specification of
' the behaviour; do not read it as one.
FUNC __collections_slice OF T(value AS List OF T, start AS Integer, stop AS Integer) AS List OF T
  MUT result AS List OF T = []
  MUT i AS Integer = start
  WHILE i < stop
    result = collections::append(result, collections::get(value, i))
    i = i + 1
  END WHILE
  RETURN result
END FUNC

' --- new functions (§6.4) -----------------------------------------------------

' Stable bottom-up merge sort keyed by keyFn. keyFn is evaluated exactly once per
' element (via transform, as before); the merge carries items and their keys in
' parallel and is stable on equal keys.
'@@MFB_BODY:sortBy@@

' bug-339 C9: take and drop are the two halves of one API — kept together here
' under the §6.4 banner (take used to sit above the internal-helpers banner).
' plan-39 A4: both are contiguous ranges delegating to __collections_slice, which
' is natively lowered as a bulk range copy; the native path clamps start into
' [0, len] and stop into [start, len], reproducing the old element-by-element
' bounds exactly: take(count) = slice(0, count) (count<0 or >len both collapse the
' same way), drop(count) = slice(count, len). Do not read the dead MFBASIC
' __collections_slice body as the spec of that clamping.
'@@MFB_BODY:take@@

'@@MFB_BODY:drop@@

' __collections_reduceRight was removed here: `reduceRight` is now lowered as a
' native member (plan-86-B, B2), the reverse-walk twin of native `reduce`, so it
' no longer needs an interpreted source-generic body. This comment is kept at the
' deleted body's exact line span so the source lines of every generic below are
' unchanged, keeping the `.ir` goldens of every `collections`-importing fixture
' byte-identical except for the genuine `reduceRight` call-target change. See
' `lower_collection_reduce_right_call` in
' `src/target/shared/code/builder_collection_queries.rs`.
' (line-span preserved: 9 comment lines + 1 blank == the removed 10-line body.)

'@@MFB_BODY:any@@

'@@MFB_BODY:all@@

'@@MFB_BODY:findIndex@@

'@@MFB_BODY:findLastIndex@@

'@@MFB_BODY:groupBy@@

'@@MFB_BODY:mapValues@@

'@@MFB_BODY:flatten@@

