' ─── Set algebra (plan-63-C) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
' Eight source generics over B's native Set primitives (`add`/`contains`/
' `toList`/`FOR EACH`). Pure: each returns a new value and mutates no argument.
' Instantiated only for comparable `T`, since `Set OF T` already requires it.

' Build a set from a list's distinct elements (first-occurrence order).
'@@MFB_BODY:toSet@@

' Every element of `a` and `b` (add is idempotent, so duplicates collapse).
'@@MFB_BODY:union@@

' Every element present in both `a` and `b`.
'@@MFB_BODY:intersection@@

' Every element of `a` not present in `b`.
'@@MFB_BODY:difference@@

' Every element in exactly one of `a` or `b` (an inline two-pass fold).
'@@MFB_BODY:symmetricDifference@@

' TRUE iff every element of `a` is in `b`.
'@@MFB_BODY:isSubset@@

' TRUE iff every element of `b` is in `a` (isSubset with arguments swapped).
'@@MFB_BODY:isSuperset@@

' TRUE iff `a` and `b` share no element.
'@@MFB_BODY:isDisjoint@@
